To fix the CORS (Cross-Origin Resource Sharing) error in Next.js running on WordPress, you can follow these steps:

1. Install the `cors` middleware package in your Next.js project using npm or yarn:

   ```bash
   npm install cors
   ```

2. Import the `cors` middleware in your `pages/_app.js` file:

   ```javascript
   import Cors from 'cors';

   const cors = new Cors({
     methods: ['GET', 'HEAD'],
   });

   function MyApp({ Component, pageProps }) {
     return (
       <>
         <Component {...pageProps} />
         {/* Add cors middleware to all requests */}
         <Cors />
       </>
     );
   }

   export default MyApp;
   ```

3. Modify the `cors` middleware options to fit your specific use case, such as allowing additional HTTP methods or specifying allowed origins. For more information and available options, refer to the official Cors documentation: https://github.com/expressjs/cors#configuration-options

4. Restart your Next.js development server to apply the changes.

By implementing this solution, you will be able to make cross-origin requests from your Next.js app running on WordPress without encountering CORS errors. Note that this implementation is just an example, and you may need to modify it based on your specific requirements.

